4 Proposed Framework
In this section, we define a powerful Graph Neural Network(GNN) in the hyperbolic space. We show that it can distinguish different graph structures by mapping them to different embeddings in the hyperboloid model and is as powerful as the WL test.
4.1 Overview
Theorem 1. Let G1 = (V1, E1) and G2 = (V2, E2) be two graphs. Consider a smooth Lorentzian manifold (M, g) of constant negative curvature c < 0, where g is the Lorentzian metric tensor. Suppose we define an embedding Φ : G → M (11)
